{
  "summary": "Adds a `ReconstructMultipath` method to the `Descriptor` interface, allowing a unified multipath descriptor object to be reconstructed from its expanded single-path sibling descriptors. The reconstruction inspects the derivation paths of the sibling descriptors and reconstitutes the combined multipath expression. Unit tests, negative invalid-path tests, and fuzzing harness updates are added to verify round-tripping.",
  "problem": "Multipath descriptors expand into individual single-path descriptors, but there is no mechanism to invert this expansion and recover the original unified multipath descriptor from those expanded instances.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This expansion is reversible - given the expansion in the order of the multipath elements, it is possible to determine what the original multipath descriptor was. This PR adds ReconstructMultipath to produce a new Descriptor representing the multipath descriptor that produced the expansion.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36442"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "This PR is stacked on PR #36442 and includes its commits; only the final four commits implement and test the multipath reconstruction functionality.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased onto the latest commit stack of #36442, which introduces `KeyPathElement` and changes `Parse` to return a single `std::unique_ptr<Descriptor>`; the reconstruction logic itself remains the same.",
  "card": "Adds ReconstructMultipath to reconstruct a single multipath descriptor object from an ordered set of its expanded single-path descriptors. This makes descriptor expansion reversible in memory for descriptor-aware tooling and wallet flows. The change is backed by unit tests, invalid-input tests, and fuzz testing. Depends on #36442.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": [
      "wallet",
      "rpc_api",
      "tests"
    ],
    "why": "A flaw in multipath reconstruction could produce incorrect derivation paths or invalid descriptors, potentially causing wallet derivation errors or script pubkey mismatches."
  }
}
